<title>UK: UK's Clarke raises tax on cigarettes by 15p/pack.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke raises tax on cigarettes by 15p/pack.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said Britain would increase tax on a packet of 20 cigarettes by 15 pence, by seven pence on a pack of small cigars and eight pence on a packet of pipe tobacco.</p>
<p>Clarke said this was in line with a commitment to raise tobacco duty by more than the rate of inflation each year.</p>
<p>But he said he would limit the rise on hand rolling tobacco to the rate of inflation.</p>
<p>&quot;Hand rolling tobacco is proving to be by far the easiest tobacco product to smuggle, although it represents a very small part of the market,&quot; Clarke said in his budget speech.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
